{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3453","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3453","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3453\",\"parent_revision\":\"1418b65f3d7f63c6d578ac2ce5cc55dc39f50ecec45144dfad2c335850b012eb\",\"root_revision\":\"1418b65f3d7f63c6d578ac2ce5cc55dc39f50ecec45144dfad2c335850b012eb\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-09-06\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nWhen a check runs across many artifacts, its output is a list of individual findings. The reader then works the list. Nothing in the output says whether the failures are independent or whether one cause produced all of them, so a rule that cannot be reached from where the work happens is indistinguishable from many careless authors.\\n\\n## The required behaviour\\n\\nAny check that runs over an artifact set reports the rate and the shape distribution, and a rate under a threshold routes to a rule-placement finding, never to a per-item work queue. That belongs in the review and verify skills' output contract, where it is read every time.\\n\\n## Evidence that the current shape misleads\\n\\nMeasured across the 21 backlog items filed in one session against `create/scope.md`:\\n\\n- `**Hypothesis**:` \u2014 **0 of 21**\\n- `**User-provided context**:` written unbolded \u2014 **15 of 21**, all failing the same way\\n\\nBoth were read as work queues and fixed item by item. A 0% compliance rate is not twenty-one careless authors; it is evidence the rule is unreachable from where items are written. The second is the same signal at 71% compliance.\\n\\nThree further sets in the same session carried the same character and were also read as queues rather than as findings: 27 active-task records in five incompatible key shapes; `items.pid` populated in zero rows of the dispatch database; and the escape counts across seven per-plugin items, every one produced by a scanner exempting the class it exists to catch.\\n\\n## Refinement to the routing rule\\n\\nRoute on **shape uniformity** first and rate second. Fifteen items failing the same way is a reachability signal at any rate. Fifteen items failing in fifteen different ways is a diligence signal at the same rate. Rate alone would classify both identically.\\n\\n**User-provided context**: the repo owner's framing \u2014 \\\"Rates route to reachability. Any check that runs over an artifact set reports the rate and the shape distribution, and a rate under a threshold routes to a rule-placement finding, never to a per-item work queue. That belongs in the review and verify skills' output contract, where it is read every time.\\\"\\n\\n## Open question for grooming\\n\\nThe threshold is unstated, and the refinement above argues the primary key should be the distribution rather than the rate. Which checks are in scope is also undecided \u2014 the review and verify skills are named, but the scanners (`audit_runtime_escapes.py`, the self-containment checks) produce the same kind of output and are not covered by that placement.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Repo owner, session melodic-plotting-emerson, 2026-09-06\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-09-06\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Open Question For Grooming\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nThe threshold is unstated, and the refinement above argues the primary key should be the distribution rather than the rate. Which checks are in scope is also undecided \u2014 the review and verify skills are named, but the scanners (`audit_runtime_escapes.py`, the self-containment checks) produce the same kind of output and are not covered by that placement.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Refinement To The Routing Rule\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRoute on **shape uniformity** first and rate second. Fifteen items failing the same way is a reachability signal at any rate. Fifteen items failing in fifteen different ways is a diligence signal at the same rate. Rate alone would classify both identically.\\n\\n**User-provided context**: the repo owner's framing \u2014 \\\"Rates route to reachability. Any check that runs over an artifact set reports the rate and the shape distribution, and a rate under a threshold routes to a rule-placement finding, never to a per-item work queue. That belongs in the review and verify skills' output contract, where it is read every time.\\\"\\n</div>\\n\\n## The Required Behaviour\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAny check that runs over an artifact set reports the rate and the shape distribution, and a rate under a threshold routes to a rule-placement finding, never to a per-item work queue. That belongs in the review and verify skills' output contract, where it is read every time.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Evidence That The Current Shape Misleads\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nMeasured across the 21 backlog items filed in one session against `create/scope.md`:\\n\\n- `**Hypothesis**:` \u2014 **0 of 21**\\n- `**User-provided context**:` written unbolded \u2014 **15 of 21**, all failing the same way\\n\\nBoth were read as work queues and fixed item by item. A 0% compliance rate is not twenty-one careless authors; it is evidence the rule is unreachable from where items are written. The second is the same signal at 71% compliance.\\n\\nThree further sets in the same session carried the same character and were also read as queues rather than as findings: 27 active-task records in five incompatible key shapes; `items.pid` populated in zero rows of the dispatch database; and the escape counts across seven per-plugin items, every one produced by a scanner exempting the class it exists to catch.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"1b2e16722386812996193e8f11175e4443d7d5a30d054a48e199640dc62e9a8f\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABTSAZZA\"}"}